  "question": "Regional Management System Description:\n\nThe Regional Management System is designed to manage regional information nationwide. The system encompasses multiple regions, each distinctively identified by a set of Attributes including unique Regional Code, City Code, Center Coordinates, Regional Level, Merged Name, Regional Name, Parent Regional ID, Pinyin, Abbreviation, and Postal Code.  A hierarchical structure among regions is established through Parent Regional ID, supporting the management of multi-level regional structures.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0319\n\nCREATE TABLE `region` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `regional_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `city_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `center_longitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `center_latitude` decimal(10,6) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `regional_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `merged_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `regional_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_regional_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pinyin` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `abbreviation` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `region_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_regional_id`) REFERENCES `region` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
